WEBVTT

00:30.690 --> 00:32.330
Can I do, do?

01:33.460 --> 01:35.770
I want to see the ocean.

01:38.060 --> 01:41.010
I want to fall in love with someone.

01:59.650 --> 02:01.380
It's delicious!

02:01.380 --> 02:05.850
No matter how many times I have it,
the strawberry parfait never fails to impress!

02:05.850 --> 02:09.260
Right, what should I get for food later?

02:09.260 --> 02:10.160
Huga.

02:10.160 --> 02:14.700
I had Japanese yesterday.
The time before that was Chinese...

02:14.700 --> 02:18.400
I know, how does Italian sound?

02:18.400 --> 02:20.040
Huga.

02:21.100 --> 02:22.770
That settles that!

02:22.770 --> 02:28.720
Okay, we'll go shopping for fish, pasta, olive oil...

02:30.280 --> 02:32.210
Speaking of Italian...

02:32.210 --> 02:33.410
Gelato!

02:33.420 --> 02:34.420
Tiramisu!

02:34.420 --> 02:36.050
Pan na cotta!

02:36.050 --> 02:39.900
Please accept our amore!

02:45.190 --> 02:46.830
Huga...

02:52.300 --> 02:56.110
Oh, how surprising, an android.

03:02.140 --> 03:04.020
H..Hold on a second!

03:06.250 --> 03:08.680
Hey, can you wait just a second?

03:08.680 --> 03:13.360
I was hoping you could tell me where
I can find someone to repair me.

03:15.520 --> 03:17.160
Huga?

03:23.400 --> 03:25.810
F..Forgive my intrusion.

03:26.070 --> 03:29.670
I had no idea that a princess was residing here.

03:29.670 --> 03:31.880
It's fine, be at ease.

03:34.940 --> 03:38.550
But it's rare to encounter an android,

03:38.550 --> 03:43.020
and even more rare to find one living
alone amongst humans.

03:45.090 --> 03:46.990
Do you have a name?

03:46.990 --> 03:50.560
It's Ciel, I gave myself that name.

03:53.360 --> 03:55.200
Very well.

03:55.200 --> 03:58.670
Your body seems to be quite damaged.

03:58.670 --> 04:01.940
I'll allow you to stay here while we perform
the necessary maintenance.

04:01.940 --> 04:04.570
Oh, thank you so much.

04:04.570 --> 04:08.840
In that case, please let me work here
until the repairs are complete.

04:08.840 --> 04:10.280
As you wish.

04:10.280 --> 04:12.480
Flandre, take him with you.

04:12.480 --> 04:14.120
Huga.

04:17.450 --> 04:21.260
He's a bit scary, but he seems like a nice guy.

04:23.530 --> 04:28.530
I had no idea that there were androids
who could speak properly.

04:28.660 --> 04:30.630
I just figured all they could say was "Huga, huga".

04:30.630 --> 04:33.700
Are you sure it's okay to have
someone like that around?

04:34.300 --> 04:36.710
I'm merciful.

04:38.210 --> 04:41.210
I don't like androids at all,

04:41.210 --> 04:45.020
but your servant seemed to have
a reason for bringing him here.

04:47.550 --> 04:51.690
One android can understand what another
android is going through.

04:51.690 --> 04:53.320
Hiro...

04:55.190 --> 04:59.070
Say, Hime, why do I have to serve you your meal?

04:59.830 --> 05:02.600
Because Sawawa hasn't made it home yet.

05:02.900 --> 05:07.010
Go pick her up, the sun will set soon.

05:13.240 --> 05:16.340
Your master is quite frightening.

05:16.340 --> 05:18.110
That sharp gleam in her eyes...

05:18.110 --> 05:21.720
It was almost as if she can read
through everything.

05:21.720 --> 05:23.250
Huga, huga.

05:23.250 --> 05:28.060
I know, it will probably take a few
days just to repair my face.

05:28.060 --> 05:31.090
Also, there are other parts of me
that are damaged as well.

05:33.300 --> 05:35.940
Aren't you going to ask about me?

05:39.700 --> 05:41.340
Huga.

05:43.440 --> 05:46.750
You're kind, Flandre.

05:49.580 --> 05:53.050
She has an android staying with her?

05:53.050 --> 05:56.960
And he's working as live-in help?

05:58.220 --> 05:59.590
I see.

05:59.590 --> 06:01.690
So, you've lost your job and have nowhere to go,

06:01.690 --> 06:06.260
so you decided to ask me to help
because of my kind heart.

06:06.960 --> 06:09.030
That's how it happened, right?

06:10.830 --> 06:14.340
No! How did you jump to such a conclusion?

06:14.340 --> 06:17.870
Get off of me! I said, get off!

06:17.870 --> 06:20.320
It's nothing to be ashamed of.

06:25.610 --> 06:31.160
They say that your loved one appears
when you're down on your luck.

06:32.020 --> 06:36.530
What?! You sent Francesca
to drag me here against my will!

06:37.890 --> 06:40.190
No matter how many servants I have around me,

06:40.200 --> 06:42.830
it's all worth nothing to me
if my number one isn't around.

06:42.830 --> 06:46.140
These fellas here missed you, too!

06:48.440 --> 06:50.070
You're such a stubborn one.

06:50.070 --> 06:52.540
You know you prefer me to my sister.

06:52.540 --> 06:56.840
You know you feel more at home at my mansion.

06:56.850 --> 06:59.110
Why can't you admit your true feelings?

06:59.110 --> 07:01.820
Do whatever you want with him, guys.

07:04.090 --> 07:08.930
I... I have to pick up my sister!

07:10.290 --> 07:13.490
I can't eat another bite.

07:13.500 --> 07:15.130
Ah...

07:21.900 --> 07:23.400
I'm off!

07:23.410 --> 07:25.390
Have a nice trip.

07:28.410 --> 07:29.980
Huga, huga.

07:29.980 --> 07:32.120
Ah, my apologies.

07:34.720 --> 07:37.890
That's good, he does seem like a nice guy.

08:00.640 --> 08:02.780
Not bad.

08:04.510 --> 08:06.210
Thank you so much.

08:06.210 --> 08:09.980
You sure have learned fast.

08:09.990 --> 08:14.990
Ciel is very talented.
He's also a hard worker and very nice.

08:15.020 --> 08:16.870
You're too kind.

08:19.160 --> 08:23.070
I'm glad the princess has taken a liking to me.

08:23.930 --> 08:26.200
Thank you, Flandre.

08:26.200 --> 08:27.430
Huga?

08:27.440 --> 08:29.280
It's all thanks to you.

08:35.510 --> 08:37.180
I'll show you something nifty.

08:37.180 --> 08:38.780
Huga?

08:39.010 --> 08:43.120
It's just a shell, but it's a valuable treasure to me.

08:43.850 --> 08:46.560
Here, put it to your ear, like this.

08:51.230 --> 08:54.260
Can you hear it?
Can you hear the ocean?

08:58.470 --> 09:00.410
I had just escaped.

09:05.410 --> 09:10.520
Three years ago, I worked as a miner in a
deuterium mine in the Royal Kingdom.

09:11.610 --> 09:13.420
But I escaped.

09:28.730 --> 09:31.510
Day after day, I continued walking...

09:32.230 --> 09:34.040
And then...

09:42.480 --> 09:44.460
I saw the ocean.

09:53.090 --> 09:57.560
I can't put into words how I felt at that moment.

10:05.930 --> 10:10.580
Have you ever seen the ocean, Flandre?

10:12.570 --> 10:15.520
The truth is that we're free!

10:32.190 --> 10:35.270
Go, my soldiers!

10:40.600 --> 10:43.140
Hey! What's with that attitude?!

10:43.140 --> 10:45.010
You call yourselves soldiers?!

10:45.010 --> 10:47.510
Put some effort into it! Effort!

10:48.910 --> 10:52.550
The more I look at these dogs,
the dumber they look.

10:52.980 --> 10:55.480
But they seem to like each other.

10:55.480 --> 11:00.050
The reason they're advancing slowly is
because of how short their legs are.

11:00.050 --> 11:01.790
Damn it...

11:01.790 --> 11:03.770
This isn't some show!

11:05.030 --> 11:06.930
What are you so angry for?

11:06.930 --> 11:10.230
I came to observe because you said you're
training them to be sacred warriors.

11:10.230 --> 11:13.930
Observe?! You're just here to make fun of me!

11:13.940 --> 11:16.800
But the weather is also fabulous.

11:16.800 --> 11:19.370
Come on, take a break.

11:19.370 --> 11:21.710
Don't break for lunch!

11:21.710 --> 11:24.110
Beth, Tippet, Pochi!

11:24.110 --> 11:26.450
I brought some for you, too.

11:26.450 --> 11:29.090
Don't make up names for them!

11:33.320 --> 11:35.760
Damn, you guys!

11:35.760 --> 11:39.760
Damn it! Have some pride as a soldier!

11:42.860 --> 11:44.840
Thank you for everything.

11:49.070 --> 11:51.310
The time is just about right.

11:51.740 --> 11:56.380
Is the time ripe to start,
just like this Romanee Conti?

11:56.950 --> 11:59.430
Are you up to something again?

12:01.250 --> 12:04.350
A grotesque gathering, rife with bad taste.

12:04.350 --> 12:05.850
Oh, Ms. Reiri.

12:05.850 --> 12:06.850
Have you come again to...

12:06.850 --> 12:12.630
Have you come to interrupt the Meister's
marvelous, fabulous show, you sly witch?!

12:12.830 --> 12:14.490
I came to say hello.

12:14.500 --> 12:17.460
I'm actually a huge fan.

12:17.470 --> 12:20.140
I love to watch you shamelessly
pretend to be high-brow.

12:21.340 --> 12:22.870
So, you've...

12:22.870 --> 12:27.870
You can't possibly grasp the artistic merit
of the Meister's almighty works!

12:28.340 --> 12:31.320
You should be ashamed, you anemic little girl!

12:33.080 --> 12:34.850
Whatever.

12:34.850 --> 12:35.880
In any case...

12:35.880 --> 12:38.490
You're still talking? Are you?!

12:38.490 --> 12:41.860
Shut up! You annoy me!

12:41.860 --> 12:44.770
Get out of my sight!

12:49.360 --> 12:53.930
As I was saying, I plan on observing
you very closely this time.

12:53.940 --> 12:56.540
I shall show you a masterpiece.

13:01.040 --> 13:03.220
According to Flandre's report, Ciel,

13:03.650 --> 13:08.650
the SEN, the Synapse Emulation Network,
within your head,

13:09.420 --> 13:12.230
is quite damaged due to years of deterioration.

13:13.390 --> 13:15.190
You have about one year left.

13:15.190 --> 13:17.690
Or you can perform daily maintenance.

13:17.690 --> 13:19.500
What do you want to do?

13:20.260 --> 13:25.040
I have no intention of finding out what your
reason is for coming to the human world.

13:28.400 --> 13:33.110
However, if you return to the Royal Kingdom, they
will have the engineers and parts that you need.

13:34.010 --> 13:35.890
Decide for yourself.

13:38.750 --> 13:43.020
For offering such kindness
to a lowly machine such as myself,

13:43.020 --> 13:45.830
I am extremely grateful, Your Majesty.

13:46.150 --> 13:48.900
I will leave here tomorrow morning.

13:50.290 --> 13:53.530
Throughout my travels, I've discovered
what it means to be free.

13:53.530 --> 13:57.500
They will erase my memories
if I return to the Royal Kingdom.

13:58.000 --> 14:00.600
My memories are my soul.

14:00.600 --> 14:03.510
Therefore, I will continue on my journey.

14:05.570 --> 14:10.570
Do whatever you want.

14:16.220 --> 14:17.860
Huga.

14:18.450 --> 14:20.330
This is goodbye.

14:21.260 --> 14:25.230
I'll be fine, you needn't worry about me.

14:25.630 --> 14:27.260
Huga?

14:28.730 --> 14:32.370
It's fine, I want you to keep it.

14:32.370 --> 14:34.180
And also,

14:34.270 --> 14:38.110
please don't forget about me, Flandre.

14:40.910 --> 14:43.290
I suppose it's time to raise the curtain.

15:05.930 --> 15:07.570
Huga!

15:13.170 --> 15:15.590
Thought I'd give it a shot.

15:18.250 --> 15:20.910
You aren't bad by nature,

15:20.920 --> 15:24.230
but there's one thing that didn't sit right with me.

15:24.720 --> 15:27.220
I'm referring to freedom.

15:27.220 --> 15:31.530
I've never once met an android
that could understand freedom.

15:32.830 --> 15:34.490
Huga!

15:41.570 --> 15:44.070
You can pick up Flandre?
She weighs multiple tons!

15:44.070 --> 15:45.710
Huga!

15:46.410 --> 15:48.050
Flandre!

15:49.740 --> 15:51.550
Huga...

15:53.850 --> 15:55.950
What the hell's going on?

16:04.630 --> 16:06.260
Ciel...

16:09.860 --> 16:11.260
Why?

16:11.270 --> 16:13.580
It's fine, Liza.

16:14.540 --> 16:16.100
What does she mean by that?

16:16.100 --> 16:19.510
Physical attacks won't be effective
against an android.

16:19.510 --> 16:22.040
There's no way we can stop him.

16:22.880 --> 16:24.520
Hime!

16:31.750 --> 16:34.590
He never listens.

16:34.590 --> 16:38.430
But how do we stop that mechanical doll?

16:38.430 --> 16:40.570
Isn't it obvious?

16:45.170 --> 16:47.830
So, you finally arrived, Sherwood.

16:47.840 --> 16:52.180
It's not nice to summon someone
this late at night, Sister.

17:00.550 --> 17:04.350
Well now, you malfunctioning android,

17:04.350 --> 17:06.190
unlike my sister's tiny maid,

17:06.190 --> 17:11.300
my Francesca is outfitted with a battle subroutine.

17:11.760 --> 17:13.090
Francesca!

17:13.090 --> 17:14.730
Huga.

17:34.150 --> 17:37.390
Seems things didn't go as planned, huh?

17:37.750 --> 17:41.860
You probably inserted a virus into that android,

17:42.420 --> 17:44.730
but it wasn't a very good one.

17:45.360 --> 17:50.000
It seems you are unable to appreciate
the quality of my art.

17:51.270 --> 17:52.730
A virus?

17:52.730 --> 17:56.510
Did you really think I'd resort to
something that pathetic?

17:58.070 --> 18:02.110
There will come a day when you'll appreciate
the aesthetics of my work,

18:02.110 --> 18:05.820
along with the frustration of knowing
I tasted the princesses' blood before you.

18:06.910 --> 18:09.830
Well then, allow me to enjoy the ride.

18:23.860 --> 18:26.230
How's it going over there, Francesca?

18:26.230 --> 18:27.870
Huga, huga.

18:27.970 --> 18:30.780
I see, how ironic.

18:31.310 --> 18:34.270
Ciel is near the end of his life and yet,
we're able to repair him,

18:34.280 --> 18:37.640
while we lack the pans to repair Flandre.

18:37.650 --> 18:39.630
No way...

18:41.920 --> 18:47.060
Sister, there are some interesting remnants
in Ciel's memory stack.

18:47.520 --> 18:49.560
According to the data we recovered,

18:49.560 --> 18:54.910
he has twenty-seven years of service
recorded since he was activated.

18:55.100 --> 18:59.430
But he's actually only been in operation
for the last ten days.

18:59.430 --> 19:01.500
What does that mean?

19:01.500 --> 19:06.500
It means someone illicitly forged all of his
memories from the time before he met Flandre.

19:08.380 --> 19:09.880
Your Majesty...

19:10.980 --> 19:12.650
You were awake?

19:12.650 --> 19:14.710
I activated him a few minutes ago.

19:14.720 --> 19:17.560
I figured he'd want to know about himself.

19:18.250 --> 19:21.890
I have made irreparable mistakes.

19:23.020 --> 19:25.890
I don't care what becomes of me.

19:25.890 --> 19:32.280
So, please use my pans to save Flandre.

19:38.110 --> 19:40.980
I've only been alive for ten days anyway.

19:45.380 --> 19:47.790
There's nothing you'd want to do over?

19:53.050 --> 19:58.500
General Hospital

20:06.870 --> 20:09.680
Are you the one who's behind all this?

20:10.500 --> 20:13.350
Call me the Creator.

20:20.650 --> 20:22.220
It's useless.

20:22.220 --> 20:25.960
I've removed the cancel switch.

20:28.690 --> 20:30.490
Answer me.

20:30.490 --> 20:33.790
Did you create all of my memories?

20:33.790 --> 20:36.270
Yes, I composed all of them.

20:38.800 --> 20:42.570
Then the ocean and that shell...

20:42.570 --> 20:46.040
They were props, props for the play.

20:48.440 --> 20:51.750
Your life is a novel that I wrote.

20:52.050 --> 20:56.120
Your entire existence is a work of fiction.

20:56.120 --> 20:57.780
You...

20:57.790 --> 21:01.730
You are the worst...

21:08.330 --> 21:10.310
I want to see the ocean.

21:11.270 --> 21:14.370
I want to fall in love with someone.

21:31.020 --> 21:33.000
I'm taking off!

23:41.820 --> 23:42.880
Huga.

23:42.880 --> 23:45.290
Flandre, I have a favor to ask you.

23:45.290 --> 23:46.290
Huga?

23:46.290 --> 23:49.720
Can you call me big brother?

23:49.720 --> 23:50.290
Huga?

23:51.930 --> 23:52.960
I mean, all I have is an older sister.

23:52.960 --> 23:56.060
I've always thought it would be nice
to have a little sister, too.

23:56.060 --> 23:58.030
Come on, say it!

23:58.030 --> 23:59.270
Huga.

23:59.270 --> 24:01.940
H..Hime! How long have you been standing there?

24:01.940 --> 24:03.870
Having fun, Hiro?

24:03.870 --> 24:06.640
N..Next episode, "Princess Cat Tongue"

24:06.640 --> 24:07.910
Don't look at me like that, Hime!

24:08.910 --> 24:10.290
Huga, huga.
